WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.245 --> 00:00:02.029
- Good morning, Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:02.029 --> 00:00:04.885
My one word is "believe,"
and I believe in people

00:00:04.885 --> 00:00:06.738
more than they believe in themselves.

00:00:06.738 --> 00:00:07.671
And my sincere hope is that

00:00:07.671 --> 00:00:10.494
if you see in yourself what I see in you,

00:00:10.494 --> 00:00:12.249
you'll be able to change the planet.

00:00:12.249 --> 00:00:13.438
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:13.438 --> 00:00:17.070
today's message is "solve big problems."

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.444
Over to you, Jack Ma.

00:00:18.444 --> 00:00:20.333
(rooster crowing)

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:23.320
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.078
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:26.078 --> 00:00:30.381
♫ I wake up every morning ♫

00:00:30.381 --> 00:00:34.257
- We are not a company
that normally China call.

00:00:34.257 --> 00:00:37.182
We call ourselves a
company running a platform.

00:00:37.182 --> 00:00:41.029
A company that is running an ecosystem.

00:00:41.029 --> 00:00:42.255
We are almost everywhere.

00:00:42.255 --> 00:00:46.365
People say, "Jack, you know
you're in the B2B, B2C,

00:00:46.365 --> 00:00:49.630
"and you're calling C2B on a
finance and online payment,

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:53.180
"logistic, cloud computing,
you are everywhere."

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.737
Not because we are greedy,
not because we want to do it.

00:00:55.737 --> 00:00:56.786
Because we have to do it.

00:00:56.786 --> 00:00:58.963
If we cannot, if we do not do it,

00:00:58.963 --> 00:01:02.422
China e-commerce in the
years will collapse.

00:01:02.422 --> 00:01:06.497
I remember nine years ago,
when I started Alipay.

00:01:06.497 --> 00:01:09.510
People say, "Jack, don't
touch the financing sector

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.927
"cause it's illegal, you may imprisoned."

00:01:14.838 --> 00:01:18.446
And we thought to ourselves,
if we don't do it,

00:01:18.446 --> 00:01:22.798
the China e-commerce will
always like a chat room.

00:01:22.798 --> 00:01:24.273
Everybody say it's a good thing.

00:01:24.273 --> 00:01:26.507
"I don't pay, you don't get the things."

00:01:26.507 --> 00:01:28.914
So I say, "Well, put me in the prison.

00:01:28.914 --> 00:01:33.084
"Let's make sure that Alipay,
the payment solution works."

00:01:33.084 --> 00:01:34.550
And the people said the payment solution

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.958
is such a stupid idea,
it's an escort service.

00:01:37.958 --> 00:01:40.667
I pay you, you hold the
money and you get the things.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:41.742
You pay the money, if you don't get

00:01:41.742 --> 00:01:43.772
the things you want, return the money.

00:01:43.772 --> 00:01:46.184
They said, "It's a stupid product."

00:01:46.184 --> 00:01:49.162
and I say, "As long as it
has solved the problem,

00:01:49.162 --> 00:01:51.271
"I like stupid things, you know."

00:01:51.271 --> 00:01:53.423
Let's make stupid things smart.

00:01:53.423 --> 00:01:55.426
Keep on improving everyday.

00:01:55.426 --> 00:01:58.593
Today, we have over 800 million people

00:01:59.774 --> 00:02:03.921
registered using Alipay, that's the count.

00:02:03.921 --> 00:02:06.979
And Alipay today solved
the e-commerce problem.

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:10.978
We are paying the electricity,
water bill, and even taxi.

00:02:10.978 --> 00:02:14.561
And last week I went
to a vegetable market,

00:02:15.574 --> 00:02:18.730
somebody say, "We accept Alipay."

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.028
(audience laughing)

00:02:20.028 --> 00:02:23.807
Because they say, "Alipay,
they get the false money,

00:02:23.807 --> 00:02:27.638
"and Alipay can solve that problem."

00:02:27.638 --> 00:02:31.805
So, we are actually building
up an infrastructure of China.

00:02:32.976 --> 00:02:33.809
It's hard to stay motivated

00:02:33.809 --> 00:02:35.782
when you're solving small problems.

00:02:35.782 --> 00:02:37.608
At least for me, I have a really hard time

00:02:37.608 --> 00:02:39.287
staying motivated, staying engaged

00:02:39.287 --> 00:02:42.260
if I see the problem as
really small and tiny.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:44.420
I had a call yesterday with a YouTuber

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:46.370
who has a successful channel

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:48.265
but hasn't posted in almost a year,

00:02:48.265 --> 00:02:51.881
and now she wants to get back on the horse

00:02:51.881 --> 00:02:53.363
and keep posting more videos,

00:02:53.363 --> 00:02:55.649
and she's so concerned about

00:02:55.649 --> 00:02:58.012
what happens in that first video.

00:02:58.012 --> 00:03:00.041
She has plan to make more videos

00:03:00.041 --> 00:03:02.153
but all she's wrapped up in is

00:03:02.153 --> 00:03:04.743
"What do I do with this first video?"

00:03:04.743 --> 00:03:07.080
And it's important to figure out

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.686
what happens in that first
video, but much more important is

00:03:09.686 --> 00:03:11.352
what's the consistent plan, right?

00:03:11.352 --> 00:03:13.084
If you want to have success on YouTube

00:03:13.084 --> 00:03:15.314
it's about making regular videos.

00:03:15.314 --> 00:03:18.196
How are you going to get to weekly videos

00:03:18.196 --> 00:03:20.990
and then multiple times
per week and then daily?

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:23.604
The long tail, the long term,
is so much more important

00:03:23.604 --> 00:03:27.398
than what happens in
this one specific video,

00:03:27.398 --> 00:03:29.491
because how many of your
subscribers are going to watch it,

00:03:29.491 --> 00:03:31.711
it's just not as important.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:34.714
So for me, I hate focusing
on the little things

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:37.239
when there's a much bigger
problem to focus on.

00:03:37.239 --> 00:03:38.865
She really should be focusing on,

00:03:38.865 --> 00:03:40.655
"Okay, I make a first video,
doesn't really matter."

00:03:40.655 --> 00:03:42.470
Any single video I put up on my channel,

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:43.832
it doesn't really matter,

00:03:43.832 --> 00:03:45.704
it doesn't really have a huge impact.

00:03:45.704 --> 00:03:47.894
It's accumulation, it's
every single video.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:49.726
So I want to focus on the big things,

00:03:49.726 --> 00:03:51.876
I want to focus on the big problems.

00:03:51.876 --> 00:03:55.953
I want to solve that and not
just this little tiny thing.

00:03:55.953 --> 00:03:58.330
And so it's why I want to
help a billion entrepreneurs.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.766
It's a motivating, an inspiring goal.

00:04:00.766 --> 00:04:03.215
I like helping entrepreneurs one-on-one.

00:04:03.215 --> 00:04:05.818
It gives me a lot great
personal joy and satisfaction,

00:04:05.818 --> 00:04:07.873
but I want to have a big impact,

00:04:07.873 --> 00:04:09.135
I know I can have a bigger impact,

00:04:09.135 --> 00:04:11.390
if you have the ability,
you have the responsibility,

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.360
and so that wakes me up energized

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.788
and try to go out and do something.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.747
When I'm coming here making
these videos for you,

00:04:17.747 --> 00:04:21.959
I'm imagining that I'm
speaking to a million people.

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:23.639
And I hope this message gets through,

00:04:23.639 --> 00:04:25.043
because I want to have a big impact.

00:04:25.043 --> 00:04:27.421
And so when you work on big problems,

00:04:27.421 --> 00:04:29.759
you're more motivated, I think
especially as entrepreneurs.

00:04:29.759 --> 00:04:31.571
We want to do something bigger.

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:33.621
We have that mind to want to go out

00:04:33.621 --> 00:04:34.915
and have that huge impact,

00:04:34.915 --> 00:04:39.115
and so we hate working on
these tiny, small problems.

00:04:39.115 --> 00:04:42.789
The flip side, though,
sometimes is it can be too big.

00:04:42.789 --> 00:04:44.893
And I remember having
this, where I thought,

00:04:44.893 --> 00:04:46.645
"Can I actually help a
billion entrepreneurs?

00:04:46.645 --> 00:04:48.082
"Can I actually change the world?

00:04:48.082 --> 00:04:49.207
"Like, it's a noble thing,

00:04:49.207 --> 00:04:51.019
"but can I actually go out and do it?"

00:04:51.019 --> 00:04:54.319
"And sometimes your goal can be too big.

00:04:54.319 --> 00:04:57.174
And may even depend on
the day, to be honest.

00:04:57.174 --> 00:04:58.612
Some days you wake up and you're motivated

00:04:58.612 --> 00:05:00.238
and ready and go do it, and
some days you wake up and say,

00:05:00.238 --> 00:05:01.571
"Who am I to be able to go off

00:05:01.571 --> 00:05:03.701
"and have that big of an impact?"

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:06.865
And so it's finding where is
that edge of your comfort zone

00:05:06.865 --> 00:05:09.615
What's goal that's big enough to push you,

00:05:09.615 --> 00:05:12.783
to say, "That's just beyond achievable,

00:05:12.783 --> 00:05:15.485
"if I push myself hard I
can go out and do that.

00:05:15.485 --> 00:05:17.218
"I'm at the edge of my comfort zone."

00:05:17.218 --> 00:05:19.734
Because if it's too easy,
you're not going to be

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:20.923
motivated to go out and do it.

00:05:20.923 --> 00:05:22.689
You're going to be bored,
you're going to feel like

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:24.353
it's a waste of your time,
a waste of your talent,

00:05:24.353 --> 00:05:25.955
you're not going to be engaged in it.

00:05:25.955 --> 00:05:28.150
And if it's too big or too hard,

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:29.723
you're also not going
to be motivated to do it

00:05:29.723 --> 00:05:32.216
because it's impossible and
it's never going to get done.

00:05:32.216 --> 00:05:35.880
So find what that goal is at
the edge of your comfort zone,

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.954
solving a big problem
that is meaningful to you,

00:05:37.954 --> 00:05:40.723
that is impactful to you,
that makes you feel valuable.

00:05:40.723 --> 00:05:43.909
If you can go out and reach it
and solve it and help people,

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:45.674
I think that's really,
really, really important

00:05:45.674 --> 00:05:46.764
as entrepreneurs.

00:05:46.764 --> 00:05:48.972
And I'd be looking at yourself,
your life, your business,

00:05:48.972 --> 00:05:51.273
if you don't feel challenged,
if you feel bored,

00:05:51.273 --> 00:05:53.272
if you're not growing,
it's probably because

00:05:53.272 --> 00:05:56.436
you are not solving a big
enough problem right now.

00:05:56.436 --> 00:05:57.995
So the question of the day today is,

00:05:57.995 --> 00:06:01.538
I'm curious, what is the big
problem that you want to solve

00:06:01.538 --> 00:06:03.585
right now with your business?

00:06:03.585 --> 00:06:04.856
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:06:04.856 --> 00:06:06.180
really curious to find out,

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.451
and also if you're leaving a comment

00:06:07.451 --> 00:06:09.550
within the first couple
of this video going live,

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:13.179
you have a chance to win
one of two daily prizes.

00:06:13.179 --> 00:06:14.339
I also want to give a quick shout-out

00:06:14.339 --> 00:06:15.817
to Paul-Benoit Duvoisin.

00:06:15.817 --> 00:06:17.399
Thank you so much for picking up a copy

00:06:17.399 --> 00:06:18.881
of my book, Your One Word.

00:06:18.881 --> 00:06:20.664
I really, really, really appreciate it,

00:06:20.664 --> 00:06:22.455
And I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:06:22.455 --> 00:06:23.702
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:06:23.702 --> 00:06:24.852
I believe in you,

00:06:24.852 --> 00:06:26.638
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:06:26.638 --> 00:06:29.511
and whatever your one word is, much love,

00:06:29.511 --> 00:06:32.010
and I'll see you again tomorrow
morning for another shot

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:33.685
of Entspresso.

00:06:33.685 --> 00:06:36.084
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:36.084 --> 00:06:40.251
♫ Entspresso keep me going ♫

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:45.749
- [Narrator] For Naveen, the
billionaire formula is simple.

00:06:45.749 --> 00:06:47.900
- [Naveen] What makes a successful person?

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.735
They go out and solve big problems.

00:06:50.735 --> 00:06:52.626
So you know how to make a billion dollars?

00:06:52.626 --> 00:06:55.605
You solve a 10 billion dollar problem.

00:06:55.605 --> 00:06:57.326
- [Narrator] Having
already made his billions,

00:06:57.326 --> 00:06:58.826
he unashamedly wants to use

00:06:58.826 --> 00:07:02.076
his business brain to change our world.

00:07:02.953 --> 00:07:05.365
- Let's focus on education, healthcare,

00:07:05.365 --> 00:07:08.186
energy, shortage of
water, shortage of food.

00:07:08.186 --> 00:07:11.103
And I'm going to tell you how
innovation and entrepreneurship

00:07:11.103 --> 00:07:13.505
can solve each of these problems.

00:07:13.505 --> 00:07:14.942
Let's look at education.

00:07:14.942 --> 00:07:18.600
Imagine if you're able
to use a $25 tablet,

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:22.335
and build some type of
game that is more effective

00:07:22.335 --> 00:07:25.914
than a private tutor,
and is more addictive

00:07:25.914 --> 00:07:28.431
than the most addictive video game.

00:07:28.431 --> 00:07:30.099
Think about it, one day a child

00:07:30.099 --> 00:07:31.479
is going to come to the mother and say,

00:07:31.479 --> 00:07:34.169
"Mom, can I play just
one more hour of math?

00:07:34.169 --> 00:07:36.450
"Because I enjoy it so much."

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:37.665
- [Narrator] Naveen has a knack

00:07:37.665 --> 00:07:39.769
of putting people under his spell.

00:07:39.769 --> 00:07:41.609
Making his mission to
solve some of mankind's

00:07:41.609 --> 00:07:45.876
biggest problems seem plausible
in space and on Earth.

00:07:45.876 --> 00:07:48.024
What if we can build an
artificial intelligence system

00:07:48.024 --> 00:07:50.265
that can be used by a village girl?

00:07:50.265 --> 00:07:51.744
She will be able to go door to door

00:07:51.744 --> 00:07:52.684
and able to diagnose a disease

00:07:52.684 --> 00:07:55.470
where there are no healthcare,
there's no hospitals,

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:56.897
there are no doctors.

00:07:56.897 --> 00:07:59.151
- [Narrator] These are
big ideas that could turn

00:07:59.151 --> 00:08:03.125
a big profit but some of
them seem a bit farfetched.

00:08:03.125 --> 00:08:05.771
- [Naveen] What if you take
a 3D printer on the moon?

00:08:05.771 --> 00:08:07.574
And somebody can go out and send

00:08:07.574 --> 00:08:10.263
the DNA of a bacteria or a virus

00:08:10.263 --> 00:08:11.530
and we print it right there and leave it

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:14.685
on the moon and watch it grow.

00:08:14.685 --> 00:08:16.365
- [Interviewer] These ideas,
they're a bit out there,

00:08:16.365 --> 00:08:17.411
aren't they, Naveen?

00:08:17.411 --> 00:08:19.020
Don't people think you're just a bit mad?

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:21.893
- The point is that the
reason they think it's mad

00:08:21.893 --> 00:08:25.322
because they don't know
it's already happening.

00:08:25.322 --> 00:08:27.816
The things that used to be science fiction

00:08:27.816 --> 00:08:30.217
are now becoming science reality.

00:08:30.217 --> 00:08:31.752
- And I think that for all of you,

00:08:31.752 --> 00:08:33.816
there are many areas where

00:08:33.816 --> 00:08:35.679
there's leverage available in the world,

00:08:35.679 --> 00:08:38.487
where one or two people with a good idea

00:08:38.487 --> 00:08:41.343
and a lot of hard work can
really make a difference,

00:08:41.343 --> 00:08:42.924
there's many many things like that,

00:08:42.924 --> 00:08:44.688
and it's good not to forget that,

00:08:44.688 --> 00:08:47.938
but it's good to look for those things.

00:08:48.811 --> 00:08:51.177
Google's mission is to organize
the world's information

00:08:51.177 --> 00:08:55.015
and make it universally
accessible and useful.

00:08:55.015 --> 00:08:57.767
And one of the things that surprised me,

00:08:57.767 --> 00:08:59.779
that's a very broad mission,
that's a lot of work,

00:08:59.779 --> 00:09:03.156
we're not going to achieve
it anytime soon, right.

00:09:03.156 --> 00:09:05.301
It's almost an impossible task.

00:09:05.301 --> 00:09:07.868
But it's an exciting task
and one that you can get

00:09:07.868 --> 00:09:11.743
other people excited about,
and they can help you.

00:09:11.743 --> 00:09:13.199
And one of the things
that also surprised me

00:09:13.199 --> 00:09:15.575
is that sometimes easier to do something

00:09:15.575 --> 00:09:18.865
that's harder because other
people get excited about it

00:09:18.865 --> 00:09:21.297
and you can get much more resource.

00:09:21.297 --> 00:09:23.951
You can get tremendous resources
to solve a hard problem

00:09:23.951 --> 00:09:25.815
whereas you might only get minor resources

00:09:25.815 --> 00:09:27.633
to solve a small problem.

00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:30.654
- I like to say my management style

00:09:30.654 --> 00:09:32.543
is problem-solver-in-chief.

00:09:32.543 --> 00:09:35.072
And so what I do in a given day is

00:09:35.072 --> 00:09:38.372
I have a set of problems
that need to be solved,

00:09:38.372 --> 00:09:42.647
and I start at the most
important and work my way down.

00:09:42.647 --> 00:09:44.963
And for the problems
I don't have time for,

00:09:44.963 --> 00:09:47.088
somebody else gets to solve them.

00:09:47.088 --> 00:09:50.169
If somebody's already solving a problem,

00:09:50.169 --> 00:09:51.511
I don't need to get involved

00:09:51.511 --> 00:09:53.383
if the problem's getting solved.

00:09:53.383 --> 00:09:56.875
But people go, "Wow, so your
day's just full of problems."

00:09:56.875 --> 00:09:58.904
I'm like, "Yeah, I got a lot of problems."

00:09:58.904 --> 00:10:01.255
(audience chuckling)

00:10:01.255 --> 00:10:02.997
But it's sort of like how

00:10:02.997 --> 00:10:06.458
a math professor thinks of problems.

00:10:06.458 --> 00:10:08.076
Think of a great math professor

00:10:08.076 --> 00:10:10.526
who has no math problems to solve.

00:10:10.526 --> 00:10:13.262
He's a very sad math professor.

00:10:13.262 --> 00:10:14.095
(interviewer laughing)

00:10:14.095 --> 00:10:18.136
And so, that's very much how I look at it.

00:10:18.136 --> 00:10:21.713
Solving problems, every
problem is an opportunity

00:10:21.713 --> 00:10:24.207
for innovating and being creative,

00:10:24.207 --> 00:10:25.957
and finding something new.

00:10:25.957 --> 00:10:28.583
And that's what I love to
do, and I do it every day.

